<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yenisei Kyrgyz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yenisei Kyrgyz were a Turkic people of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-river">Yenisei River</a> region in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> profile records that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qapaghan-qaghan">Qapaghan Qaghan</a> conquered the Yenisei Kyrgyz and killed their qaghan in personal combat in 710. In 840 the Kyrgyz destroyed the Uyghur Khaganate, briefly becoming the dominant power on the Mongolian steppe.</p></div>
